From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: a view mode the browser asks for comes before the saved one

Found by the conformance comparison (shell32 ebrowser, comdlg32 filedlg:
new failures against origin/main): fast-a 3258 restored a folder view's
mode from the browser's view state stream ahead of the mode or view id the
browser asks for. Wine's ExplorerBrowser and file dialog tests (which follow
Windows) create a view with a mode or VID_Details after an earlier view of
the same browser saved another mode, and expect the one asked for; with
fast-b 3705 the ExplorerBrowser keeps such a stream too. The saved mode is
now used only when the browser asks for no view of its own (FVM_AUTO or no
valid mode). fastshell32rc (3258's gate) asks FVM_AUTO for the restored
view, and checks that an asked-for mode wins.

Mutant: SG_MUTANT_VIEW_STATE_FIRST (fastshell32rc).
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shlview.c b/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
--- a/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
@@ -3944,8 +3944,17 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IShellView3_fnCreateViewWindow3(IShellView3 *iface, IShell
     This->FolderSettings.ViewMode = mode;
     This->FolderSettings.fFlags = mask & flags;
 
-    /* the view mode that the browser kept from the view before comes first */
-    if (load_view_state(This, &mode)) This->FolderSettings.ViewMode = mode;
+    /* the view mode that the browser kept from the view before, when the browser asks for no
+     * view of its own: an explicit view id or a valid mode it passes wins, as Wine's ExplorerBrowser
+     * and file dialog conformance tests show for Windows (integ-2026-10; 3258 had the saved mode first) */
+    if (!view_id && (mode < FVM_FIRST || mode > FVM_LAST)
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_VIEW_STATE_FIRST
+        || 1
+#endif
+       )
+    {
+        if (load_view_state(This, &mode)) This->FolderSettings.ViewMode = mode;
+    }
     else if (view_id)
     {
         if (IsEqualGUID(view_id, &VID_LargeIcons))
